+++ b/responses_api_agents/harbor_agent/README.md
@@ -544,7 +544,8 @@ harbor_mask_context_overflow: true                  # optional, see "Failure cla
 
 **pi** ([github.com/earendil-works/pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), `PiNemoGym`): the standalone release
 (a Bun-compiled binary, no Node) is uploaded from `pi_archive_dir` into each sandbox and only the binary and its
-`package.json` are unpacked (the image needs `tar`). The run writes pi's `models.json` (one OpenAI-compatible
+`package.json` are unpacked (the image needs `tar`); with `pi_install: mounted` the sandbox already has the release
+tree and nothing is installed. The run writes pi's `models.json` (one OpenAI-compatible
 provider at `api_base`), `settings.json` and the optional turn-budget extension into `/logs/agent/pi-agent` and
 runs `pi --print --mode json` with the tools `read`, `bash`, `edit`, `write`; the events go to `agent/pi.txt`, the
 session to `agent/pi/sessions`. For capture the adapter turns off compaction (summary calls, compact-and-retry),
@@ -573,7 +574,9 @@ harbor_agent_kwargs:
 | Option | Default | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
 | `version` | `1.5.2` | pi release. Settings, flags and the extension API were checked against this release; another one needs `pi_sha256` and a re-check. |
-| `pi_archive_dir` | required | Directory with `<version>/<asset>`. The archive's sha256 is checked once per process, and again in the sandbox if `sha256sum` is there. |
+| `pi_install` | `upload` | `upload`: the archive from `pi_archive_dir`, unpacked in the sandbox. `mounted`: the sandbox already has the release tree (e.g. a read-only volume the sandbox platform mounts into every pod); setup only checks that `pi_bin` prints `version`. |
+| `pi_bin` | none | For `mounted`: absolute path of the `pi` executable in the sandbox (its `package.json` next to it); the run calls it by this path. |
+| `pi_archive_dir` | required for `upload` | Directory with `<version>/<asset>`. The archive's sha256 is checked once per process, and again in the sandbox if `sha256sum` is there. |
 | `pi_asset` | `pi-linux-x64.tar.gz` | Release asset (glibc x86_64, built for `bun-linux-x64-baseline`: no AVX2 needed). |
 | `pi_sha256` | built in for 1.5.2 | sha256 of the archive. |
 | `pi_timeout_sec` | none | pi is ended with exit 124 after this, so its log and exit status are recorded before Harbor's agent timeout. |
